      subtitle: "Sunak's £36 billion transport pledge, and Leeds' long wait for a mass-transit system",
      dek: "The Prime Minister promises every penny of HS2's cancelled Northern leg will return to the Midlands and North — but Mayor Tracy Brabin has heard promises like this before.",
      sourceNote: "First published in <em>The Gryphon</em>, LUU. Available <a href=\"https://www.thegryphon.co.uk/2023/10/21/network-north-levelling-up-in-action-or-more-tory-distraction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a>.",
      tag: "Analysis",
      tags: ["Politics", "Economy & Business"],
      date: "2023-10-21",
      outlet: "",
      cover: "images/writing/network-north-cover.png",
      external: "",
      // Two real graphics from the original piece — a Sankey chart of
      // the HS2-savings reallocation, and a map of the cancelled 2005
