      body: [
        "<div class=\"wa-poem wa-poem--left\"><h2 class=\"reading__section\">the loom</h2><p>Furrowed, rhythms dissonant, forehead locked against reinforced glass. Gulls overskit flooded fields, trees sink into shallows waist high, boughs blackened and skyward grasping. Brute clouds behind sift slow, sinking as sand timers’ innards. White noise roils between your ears, the screech of those grains shearing glass on their descent. Your bitback nails find purchase in perspex.</p><p>Skin of your face stretched out, pulsing with a sickness. Hot. Stomach pangs as you ragdoll in your seat. Rhythmic rolling wheels below, like an engine overturning, shunting on tight rail lines. Shapes run close and blurry beyond gritsmoke shadows. Ink in darker water. Pylons and high rises reach long limbed through the clag. Fasten taut your eyes and will on rest.</p><p>Your imminent arrival by an automated voice alerted, you brave a glance: past a solar panel sea a figure toils on her patch, half-turns to watch your train progressing distant past, punnet picnic basket elbowed, free hand ahold her wide brimmed summer hat against the gusts which surge the pall. Paler keyholes brighten now surrounding suburbs, crystallise on either cheek your tears.</p></div>"
      ]
